---
/**
 * プライバシーポリシー。
 *
 * 記述は「現時点の実態」に合わせる。やっていないことを書かない、やっていることは必ず書く。
 *
 * 現在の実態（2026-10-29）:
 *   - Google アナリティクス4（Cookie あり。同意するまで保存も送信もしない：Analytics.astro / ConsentBanner.astro）
 *   - Cloudflare Pages での配信（通信記録）
 *   - 問い合わせは fam16.com のフォーム（この運営者の別サイト）。このサイトにはフォームもメール登録も無い
 *   - アフィリエイトは AFFILIATE のフラグが立つまで無い（立てたら下の該当節が表示される）
 *   - 地図・動画などの外部埋め込みは無い
 *
 * GA4 の記述は GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID の有無に、アフィリエイトの記述は hasAnyAffiliate に連動する。
 * ⚠ 解析ツール・フォーム・埋め込み・アフィリエイトを変えたら、同じコミットで本ページと PRIVACY_UPDATED を更新する。
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LOCALES, OPERATOR, GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID, PRIVACY_UPDATED, hasAnyAffiliate, type Locale } from '../../config.ts';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return LOCALES.map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }));
}
const lang = Astro.params.lang as Locale;
const ga4 = GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID !== '';
---

<Base
  locale={lang}
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What this site collects, why, which cookies it uses and only with your consent, who processes the data abroad, and how to exercise your rights."
>
  <section class="wrap legal">
    <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {PRIVACY_UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This policy explains what {OPERATOR.name} (“I”, “me”) collects when you read Wayside Japan (waysidejapan.com),
        and what happens to it. It describes what the site actually does today, and it is updated whenever that changes.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
      <dl class="info">
        <dt>Operator</dt><dd>{OPERATOR.name}</dd>
        <dt>Representative</dt><dd>{OPERATOR.representative}</dd>
        <dt>Address</dt><dd>{OPERATOR.address}, Japan</dd>
        <dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href={OPERATOR.contactUrl}>Contact form on fam16.com</a></dd>
      </dl>

      <h2>2. What is collected</h2>
      <p>This site has no accounts, no comments, no forms and no newsletter sign-up. I do not ask you for personal data here.</p>
      <ul>
        {ga4 && (
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics, only if you accept.</strong> Google Analytics 4, provided by Google (Google Ireland Limited
            for visitors in the EEA and the UK; Google LLC in the United States), records which pages are viewed, how long
            they are open, which page or site referred you, your device and browser type, and your approximate location
            (city or region level, derived from your IP address). It uses cookies to tell one browser from another.
            I use this to see which guides are read and which need work. I do not use it to identify you, and I do not
            use it for advertising.
          </li>
        )}
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting records.</strong> The site is delivered by Cloudflare, Inc. (United States). Like any web
          host, it processes your IP address, browser type and the page you requested to deliver the page and to block
          abuse.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages you send me.</strong> To send a correction or question, you use the contact form on my
          company site, fam16.com. What you type there is handled under the privacy policy of that site, which names
          the form service it uses.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your cookie choice.</strong> If you pick Accept or Reject in the cookie banner, your choice is kept in
          your own browser (local storage, key <code>wsj-consent</code>). It is not sent to me.
        </li>
      </ul>
      {hasAnyAffiliate && (
        <p>
          Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you follow one and buy, the partner tells me about the sale
          through its own tracking, which may set its own cookies once you are on the partner’s site. The partner’s
          privacy policy applies from there.
        </p>
      )}
      <p>There are no embedded maps, videos or social media widgets on this site.</p>

      <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
      {ga4 ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Nothing is stored in your browser and nothing is sent to Google Analytics until you choose <strong>Accept</strong>{' '}
            in the cookie banner. If you choose <strong>Reject</strong>, or ignore the banner, the site works the same and
            no analytics cookies are set.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you accept, Google Analytics sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_{GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>.
            They hold a random identifier and stay on your device for up to two years unless you delete them sooner.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can change your mind at any time with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer. You can also delete
            cookies in your browser, or install Google’s
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
            More on how Google uses data from sites that use its services:
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>This site does not set cookies.</p>
      )}

      <h2>4. Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        {ga4 && <li>Analytics: your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR; the equivalent under UK law). You can withdraw it at any time.</li>}
        <li>Delivering the site securely: my legitimate interest in running a safe, working website (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
        <li>Answering your messages: my legitimate interest in replying to you, or steps you asked for.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I do not sell personal data, and I do not use it for automated decisions or profiling.</p>

      <h2>5. Who else processes it, and where</h2>
      <p>
        I am based in Japan. {ga4 ? 'Google and Cloudflare' : 'Cloudflare'} process the data above on infrastructure that
        may be outside your country, including in the United States. Where the law requires a safeguard for such a
        transfer, I rely on the provider’s own commitments, such as the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or standard
        contractual clauses, which you can find in their privacy documentation. The European Commission has recognised
        Japan as providing an adequate level of data protection for commercial operators.
      </p>
      <p>I do not share personal data with anyone else, except where the law requires it.</p>

      <h2>6. How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>
        {ga4 && 'Analytics data is kept by Google for a limited period that I set in the analytics account; reports I keep are aggregated. '}
        Hosting records are kept by Cloudflare for as long as its own policy says. Messages sent through fam16.com are
        kept as long as needed to answer them, then deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may ask me to tell you what I hold about you, to correct or delete it, to
        restrict or stop using it, and to give you a copy. You can withdraw consent at any time, and you can complain to
        your local data protection authority. In Japan, the equivalent rights are set out in the Act on the Protection of
        Personal Information.
      </p>
      <p>
        To use any of them, write through the <a href={OPERATOR.contactUrl}>contact form</a>. I will confirm it is you
        and reply without undue delay. There is no charge. Because the analytics identifier is random and I cannot link it
        to a name, I can only act on it if you tell me the identifier stored in your own cookie.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Other sites</h2>
      <p>Links to other sites are outside this policy. Check each site’s own policy.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I will update this page when the site’s data handling changes, and change the date at the top. If a change would
        affect you materially, I will say so on the site before it takes effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Revision history</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>{PRIVACY_UPDATED}: first published, with Google Analytics 4 behind a cookie consent banner.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: 56px 24px;
  }
  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .legal h1 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .legal :global(.prose h2) {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .info {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8em minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 8px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 17px;
  }
  .info dt {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .info dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .info {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2px 0;
    }
    .info dd + dt {
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
